            <ArticleTitle>Revealing a Role for NMDA Receptors in Regulating STN Inputs following the Loss of Dopamine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1227-1229</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0896-6273(17)30784-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.neuron.2017.08.041</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this issue of Neuron, Chu et al. (2017) show that dopamine depletion using a 6-OHDA model causes a decrease in hyperdirect inputs from the motor cortex directly to the STN and that rescuing this loss alleviates Parkinsonian symptoms.</AbstractText>
